Spec: ServerLib

Purpose:
  Anchor the `server` crate: declare the module tree forming the diagnostic API library and
  own the crate-root re-export surface @Config, @DiagError and @AppState. The file carries no
  behaviour of its own — every item resolves through the modules it names, each specified by
  its own spec below. The lib-vs-bin boundary is the point of the split: the `server` package
  builds this lib plus a thin binary whose @main in ./main.rs owns all process startup, while
  the lib is the compile target carrying the API modules and their `cfg(test)` unit tests that
  `cargo test -p server` runs.

Owns:
  ./lib.rs

References:
  ./anonymize.sdd, ./auth.sdd, ./authz.sdd, ./config.sdd, ./discovery.sdd, ./dto.sdd,
    ./error.sdd, ./server.sdd, ./state.sdd — one per module declared by this file; each owns
    its module's behaviour.
  ./collect/children.sdd, ./collect/clusterinfo.sdd, ./collect/logs.sdd,
    ./collect/packages.sdd, ./collect/popularity_contest.sdd, ./collect/state.sdd,
    ./collect/vynilconfig.sdd — one per submodule @collect aggregates in ./collect/mod.rs.
  /linting.sdd — the static-analysis harness whose per-crate `cfg_attr` form these crate
    attributes carry.
  ./main.rs — the binary root and the crate's only consumer; thin process bootstrap, not API.

Must:
  Carry exactly the two crate attributes, in order:
    `#![cfg_attr(not(test), deny(clippy::unwrap_used, clippy::expect_used))]`
    `#![cfg_attr(not(test), warn(clippy::arithmetic_side_effects, clippy::indexing_slicing))]`
    Both lints are scoped to not(test), so the `cfg(test)` build runs without them.
  Declare @anonymize, @auth, @authz, @collect, @config, @discovery, @dto, @error, @server
    and @state as `pub mod` — all ten API modules are public; there is no private module.
  Carry exactly three name-only `pub use` re-exports at the crate root: @Config from
    @server::config, @DiagError from @server::error, @AppState from @server::state.
  Define nothing of its own — no @fn, type, constant or macro — so the crate-root surface is
    exactly the ten modules plus those three names, and any wider root surface would break the
    parent rule that the public surface moves only with this spec.
  Run no code: no @main, no side effects. Startup belongs to @main in ./main.rs — logging
    init, the rustls `ring` provider install, clap parsing of @Config, @AppState construction,
    the @run_server call and the process exit codes are all owned there; this file only has to
    keep @main's chosen import line `use server::{@config::Config, @server::run_server,
    @state::AppState}` resolving.
  Keep both package targets lint-gated: these attributes gate the lib target while ./main.rs
    carries the same pair for the bin target; dropping either leaves that target ungated.
  Serve no consumer beyond the package binary: nothing else in the workspace imports
    `server` and the package is unpublished (`publish = false` in ./Cargo.toml), so this root
    plus @main is the whole cross-target contract of the lib today.

Exposes:
  Modules @anonymize, @auth, @authz, @collect, @config, @discovery, @dto, @error, @server,
    @state — `pub mod`; behaviour of each owned by the referenced spec.
  Re-exports at crate root: @Config aliasing @server::config::Config, @DiagError aliasing
    @server::error::DiagError, @AppState aliasing @server::state::AppState.

Accepts:
  This file branches on no input — every item is a module declaration or a re-export binding.

Tasks:
  [ ] Cover the frozen root surface: the three crate-root names denote the same items as
      their module paths and the @main import of @config::Config, @server::run_server and
      @state::AppState resolves. No mapped test exists.
  [?] No consumer actually uses the root re-exports: @main.rs reaches @Config and @AppState
      through their module paths, not the root names, and in-crate code uses
      @crate::error::DiagError. Decide later whether the re-exports stay as durable API or the
      root surface shrinks to the module paths.

Done when:
  Every Scenario above has a passing mapped test in `server` and `cargo test -p server` with
    clippy and fmt are green.

Scenario: Crate-root re-exports alias the module items
  Given an @AppState, a @Config and a @DiagError named through their module paths
  When the same three are named at the crate root instead
  Then those are the same items and types, not copies or wrappers, and no other name is
    reachable at the `server` root beyond the ten modules
  No mapped test exists.
